<programme start="20261121170000 +0000" stop="20261121203000 +0000" channel="FOX 7 Miami 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Ohio State at Nebraska</sub-title><desc lang="en">The No. 14 Buckeyes (7-3, 5-2 Big Ten) face the Cornhuskers (6-4, 3-4) at Memorial Stadium. Ohio State enters after a 28-19 victory against Northwestern behind Luke Fahey, while Nebraska snapped a skid and beat Rutgers for a shutout 31-0 win.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261121203000 +0000" stop="20261122000000 +0000" channel="FOX 7 Miami 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Texas Tech at Baylor</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Baylor Bears host the No. 12 Texas Tech Red Raiders at McLane Stadium in a Big 12 matchup. Texas Tech aims for a four-game win streak after defeating Oklahoma State 52-27, while Baylor broke a two-game win streak with a 28-7 loss against BYU.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261122000000 +0000" stop="20261122020000 +0000" channel="FOX 7 Miami 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Basketball</title><sub-title lang="en">Michigan at Villanova</sub-title><desc lang="en">The No. 18 Michigan Wolverines face the Villanova Wildcats in an NCAA Division I Men&apos;s game. Michigan rides a two-game win streak with Trey McKenney, while Villanova lost 81-61 to Pittsburgh on Nov. 17 with Devin Royal in non-conference play.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Basketball</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191260_b_v8_az.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261122020000 +0000" stop="20261122053000 +0000" channel="FOX 7 Miami 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Utah at TCU</sub-title><desc lang="en">The No. 2 Utah Utes (10-0, 7-0 Big 12) visit the TCU Horned Frogs (5-5, 3-4) in Fort Worth. Undefeated Utah enters after edging Arizona 40-39 on the road, while TCU seeks back-to-back wins at home following a 20-10 victory over Kansas State.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
